{"description":"`dispatchTool` in eka-mcp was a single 670-line switch holding all 26 tools. Every case mixed three responsibilities — decode parameters, call the capability layer, marshal the result — so no tool could be read or tested without its twenty-five neighbours, in the package whose entire job is the agent-facing boundary.","impact":"Each case moved verbatim into its own handler, with `toolHandlers` as the single routing declaration; the descriptor catalog remains the source for `tools/list`. server.go drops from 2350 to 1688 lines and is reviewable per tool. No behavioural change: the existing suite passes without a single test edit, and the three cases carrying their own gates (discard's confirmation, sync_push's pull refusal and canonical-write gate, transition's canonical-write gate) kept their logic intact."}